@node "Install"
@Title "The /X ToolTypes Information          Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"

  * Please install this command as 'DOORS' so ALL /X board will user DOORS
    instead of things like DOORLIST, LIST, WHAT & DOOR... It is better for
    all of us /X freaks if we have standards.

  - THIS PART IS TAKEN FROM THE ORGiNAL /X AMIGA GUIDE AND ARE MODIFIED -
  =======================================================================
  <module>.INFO        - This ICON defines a MODULE for /X. The Name of
                         the <module> should be the same as the executing
                         in MainMenu prompt, and should be in one of the
                         three Directories. This icon should be placed
                         in the BBS:Commands/BBSCmd directory.

     The following directorys are placed under the <BBS Path>:Commands/
     path.

     a> BBSCmd     - Modules in this directory are allowed to be
                     executed from any menu prompt or MCI text file.

     b> SYSCmd     - Modules in this directory are only accessible by
                     MCI text files and internal BBS operations.

     c> CONF(x)    - Modules in this directory are allowed to be
                     executed from conference (x) menu prompt or from
                     any MCI text file in conference (x).
     d> Node(x)    - Modules in this directory are allowed to be
                     executed from node (x) menu prompts or from any
                     MCI text file in Node (x).
  - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
  The ToolTypes of the <module(s)> :

  ACCESS= <numb>       - tells /X the access level required to run this
                         module. This option is ignored for internal
                         Module options.

  INTERNAL= <command>  - Specifies if you want to have this Module the
                         same as a internal AmiExpress command. if you
                         choose this option you don`t need the following
                         tool types.

  LOCATION= <string>   - Specifies the location of the Module.

  MULTINODE=YES        - Tells /X if the module may be simultaneously
                         accessed from other nodes, this door is multinode
                         compatible. Options for this tool type
                         are <YES/NO>.

  PASSWORD= <string>   - Force the user to enter password before executing
                         this module. This option is case sensetive wich
                         means that "OK" and "Ok" is'nt the same.
                         If you want the 'C' command to be protected then
                         use this tooltype.

  PRIORITY=SAME        - Let's you set the priority of the door. If you use
                         PRIORITY=SAME, it will use the same Priority
                         that express uses. For best result of the door use
                         the 'SAME' option.

  QUICKMODE            - This simply tells AmiExpress not to run the Module
                         in question if the user has logged onto the BBS
                         using the QUICK LOGON option.
                         If you want all the users to be able to use this
                         door then disable this option by removing the
                         tooltype.

  STACK=4096           - tells /X the stacksize to use when launching this
                         module. Default is 4096. This door requires
                         4096 bytes of stack.

  TYPE=XIM               - tells /X which type of module it is to support:
                         XIM = /X Standard Module, this door is a XIM door.

  TRAPON               - This makes LOGON Output go to a Log for Error
                         Checking, you don't need this option, just
                         fragments youre hd a lot!
  =======================================================================
@EndNode
